    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111793" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλογ-ίζω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλογίσω</span> Id., but <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ps.</u>
					96(97).3
				</span></i>
			:— 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλέγω</span>
			, <i>set on fire, burn,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1199
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				LXX
			</span></i> l.c., al.: <i>singe,</i> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1233
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be set on fire, blaze, flame,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλογιζόμενον ἅλιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					95
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): <i>to be burnt up, consumed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mu.</u>
				397a29
			</span></i>: metaph., of the tongue, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Jac.</u>
				3.6
			</span></i> (
				Act.
			 and 
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>burn, blaze,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				9.24
			</span></i>.</div>
